WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
In an alcohol, the OH
group is bonded to carbon.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.040
On its own, that carbon to
oxygen bond will not break.

3
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.900
Add acid, and everything changes.

4
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.640
Heat cyclohexanol with concentrated
phosphoric acid, and cyclohexene distils off.

5
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.280
Or warm ethanol with hydrogen
bromide, and you get bromoethane.

6
00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.580
Either way, the OH group has broken away.

7
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.680
So what does acid do to an alcohol
that lets its OH group break away?

8
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:33.560
In this mission, you'll turn alcohols
into alkenes or bromo compounds,

9
00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:37.480
and see how chemists make
alcohols in the first place.

10
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:41.260
Then you'll predict the products
for alcohols you have never met.

11
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.710
Your mission: explain what acid
does that lets the OH group go.